  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For hydrogen atom, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are the wavelengths corresponding to the transitions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> respectively as shown in figure. The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>32</mn></mfrac></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ______.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0056_755aa6237056.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 181px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "27",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Wavelength corresponding to the photon emitted in transition&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;....(1)</p><p>Wavelength corresponding to the photon emitted for transition in transition&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; ....(2)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}